cosmic-nightlight (0.5.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * The app can now ship as a flatpak, which is what makes a COSMIC Store
    listing possible. Setting the screen tint needs DRM master, which no sandbox
    permission grants, so the sandboxed app reaches a privileged helper on the
    host through flatpak-spawn and pkexec instead.
  * Installing that host helper now happens by itself, on the first time the
    night light is turned on. Before it is installed every change costs a
    password prompt, so the first one is spent installing as well as applying —
    one prompt, after which there are none. Nothing to find and no setup step.
  * Add a settings row offering the same thing, for anyone who dismissed that
    prompt, and offering to replace the installed helper when a release has
    changed what the app asks of it. It appears only when there is something to
    do and disappears by itself once done.
  * The helper accepts --version, reporting the version of its command line
    rather than of the app, so the app can tell whether a helper installed by an
    earlier release still understands it. That is what keeps an update from
    asking for a password it does not need.
  * An app icon and AppStream metadata, so the app describes itself properly to
    software centers instead of borrowing a theme icon.
  * uninstall.sh now removes a flatpak install as well, un-registers the panel
    applet so the panel does not keep restarting it, and resets the screen tint
    using whichever helper it can still find.
  * Add scripts/check-version.sh, which fails a release when the version in
    Cargo.toml, debian/changelog and the AppStream metadata disagree. A stale
    metainfo version would otherwise show the previous version on the Store page
    while serving the new build, with nothing reporting an error.
  * The note about the screen briefly flickering now appears under the
    temperature slider in the settings window, not just in the applet popup.

 -- Daniel Watts <danielcwtts@gmail.com>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 18:00:00 -0500

cosmic-nightlight (0.4.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * The schedule is now honored by whichever part of the app is running, so the
    applet alone keeps the screen on schedule. Every run mode re-checks the clock
    on a shared 15-second tick and reconciles the screen against it.
  * Remove the "Start on login" toggle, which existed only to launch the
    headless daemon: with the applet doing the scheduling there is nothing left
    for it to add. Any XDG autostart entry it wrote (including a pre-rename
    "nightshift" one) is removed at startup, so upgrades stop launching a daemon
    with no setting left to turn it off. The systemd user unit is still shipped,
    still not enabled, for anyone running without the applet.
  * Schedule times are now minute-precise: From/To pick an hour, minute, and
    AM/PM (or a 24-hour clock, following the system setting), and the Schedule
    row summarizes the window. Existing whole-hour settings are read and carried
    over.
  * Fix a schedule window that ends later in the day than it starts (e.g.
    09:00 to 17:00) leaving the tint on around the clock; such a window is now a
    plain range and only one that ends earlier wraps past midnight.
  * Re-apply the tint after a resume from suspend, whose modeset drops the gamma
    LUT and previously left the night light silently off until the next
    scheduled transition.
  * Add a brightness slider to the settings window, floored at 50% so the gamma
    dimming cannot black out the screen.
  * Applies no longer block the GUI: they run on a background thread and
    coalesce, so dragging a slider or flipping the toggle can't freeze the
    applet for the second an apply takes.
  * Serialize applies across all processes with a lock and a shared record of
    what is on screen, so several noticing the same boundary cost one flicker
    instead of several, and re-applying an unchanged tint is skipped. Failures
    back off exponentially rather than retrying every tick.
  * Sliders no longer jump out from under the pointer when another process
    writes a setting mid-drag.
  * uninstall.sh now clears a systemd enablement symlink left dangling when the
    unit file is already gone.

 -- Daniel Watts <danielcwtts@gmail.com>  Wed, 29 Jul 2026 21:45:00 +0000

cosmic-nightlight (0.3.1-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix "Start on login" being ignored: the package auto-enabled the systemd
    user service, which started the daemon on every login regardless of the
    in-app toggle. The service is no longer auto-enabled (the toggle's XDG
    autostart entry is now the single source of truth), and the postinst undoes
    any prior enablement and removes the orphaned pre-rename "nightshift" unit.
  * autostart toggle now also clears legacy ("nightshift") autostart entries and
    reflects them in its state, so upgrades from the old name behave correctly.
  * uninstall.sh now stops/disables the daemon, removes the autostart entry, and
    resets the screen tint, so uninstalling no longer leaves the screen warm or a
    daemon re-tinting on the next login.

 -- Daniel Watts <danielcwtts@gmail.com>  Mon, 15 Jun 2026 16:00:00 +0000

cosmic-nightlight (0.3.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Rename the project from "Night Shift" to "Night Light" to avoid trademark
    confusion. Crates, binaries, the app ID (now io.github.cosmic_nightlight),
    desktop entries, the polkit rule, and the systemd unit are all renamed.
    NOTE: the config directory moves to
    ~/.config/cosmic/io.github.cosmic_nightlight/, so prior settings are not
    carried over automatically.
  * Add a manual on/off override that takes precedence over the schedule and
    automatically clears at the next sunset/sunrise transition.
  * Sync settings live between the applet, settings window, and daemon via a
    cosmic_config file watcher.
  * Harden the daemon: wait for the graphical session to be foreground before
    touching DRM at login, and retry failed applies with backoff instead of
    assuming success.
  * Settings window: mirror the applet's on/off toggle and temperature, show a
    schedule status line, honour the system 12/24-hour clock, and enforce a
    minimum window size.
  * Add scripts/uninstall.sh to remove installed components.

 -- Daniel Watts <danielcwtts@gmail.com>  Mon, 15 Jun 2026 12:30:00 +0000

cosmic-nightlight (0.2.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Move the GUI into a COSMIC panel applet.
    - Status-bar icon with a popup for the on/off toggle and temperature
      slider.
    - New `--settings` window for autostart, schedule mode, sunset/sunrise
      hours, and night temperature.
    - Settings are now shared via cosmic_config across the applet, settings
      window, and daemon.
    - Autostart toggle writes an XDG autostart entry that runs the daemon
      and re-applies the saved tint on login.
    - Settings window content now scrolls when the window is shrunk.

